      keyLabs: ["Ferritin trend, liver iron concentration when indicated, CBC/ANC, creatinine/eGFR, urinalysis/protein, electrolytes, AST/ALT/bilirubin, and zinc", "Cardiac, hepatic, endocrine, auditory, ocular, growth, and transfusion-burden assessment"],
      nclexTraps: ["Chelators remove excess iron; they are not treatments for low iron.", "Ferritin alone can rise with inflammation, and a falling ferritin can signal overchelation rather than uncomplicated success."],
